{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/149046-antagonistic-courts-or-entitlements","id":149046,"title":"Antagonistic Courts or Entitlements?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-25T18:09:19-07:00","id":149046,"title":"Antagonistic Courts or Entitlements?","content":"I'm very new to CtL (running my first game here in a few weeks) and was curious if there are any established Courts or entitlements that would be considered antagonistic to a standard freehold/court system? Something similar I suppose to the Shadow Court from Dreaming. I am toying with the idea about something like this starting to foster in the local freehold and be a behind the scenes thing that eventually the players uncover. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/695-kenshin138","name":"kenshin138","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T19:51:03-07:00","id":149089,"title":"","content":"There's the Sun and Moon Courts, whose respective emotions are Disgust and Shame. They're most common in Slavic nations, I think, but have some very cool stuff going on; the Sun Court is full of massive assholes who want to judge everyone, while the Moon Court just enjoys reveling in being disgusting monsters. I'm quite fond of them both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T22:16:29-07:00","id":149141,"title":"","content":"There isn't really anything outright like that, as different freeholds can have very different interactions between courts - one freehold might be stuck in a civil war between summer/spring and winter/autumn, another has the seasonal courts united against the army of hobs that are assaulting them, a third has a cold war between the seasonals and the directional courts holed up in Chinatown. <br /> <br /> That said, there are two types of character which any &quot;right-minded&quot; Lost would be opposed to on general principles: Loyalists (who still work for their Keepers) or privateers (who kidnap people to sell to the Others for personal gain). You could easily have a band of one or the other (or both) have infiltrated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T22:32:07-07:00","id":149154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/149046-antagonistic-courts-or-entitlements?p=149141#post149141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't really anything outright like that, as different freeholds can have very different interactions between courts - one freehold might be stuck in a civil war between summer/spring and winter/autumn, another has the seasonal courts united against the army of hobs that are assaulting them, a third has a cold war between the seasonals and the directional courts holed up in Chinatown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; my current chronicle revolves around an imminent assault by a Charlatan and one of the character's responses to this crisis was to take the Summer crown, rally Spring to his side, and plunge the freehold into a military dictatorship for a short time. Winter is opposing them via a cold (ha!) war, while Autumn is doing its best to play both sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T22:52:10-07:00","id":149160,"title":"","content":"The Anti-Gentrification League (Victorian Lost) and Phantom Tong (Winter Masques) both count. The AGL is a Victorian thing but could still exist. The Phantom Tong is more a Directional Court problem than Seasonal Court, but there is nothing stopping them from setting up shop in Seasonal Court territory.<br /> <br /> Loyalists and Privateers also work well, and are possibly better choices depending on when and were the game is set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T00:42:20-07:00","id":149202,"title":"","content":"Check the index in my sig for the Sorrority of Stepsisters. They're an entire Entitlement who's job is to steal the antagonistic role from the real antagonists and then loose to the heroes.<br /> <br /> A good way to think of them is to start the game with both a real antagonist (e.g. a baby stealing True Fae) and a Stepsister who's running around leading false clues saying she's the baby thief. If the players fall for the fakes, then it turns out she actually was the thief all along because of freaky fate reasons and the players can find the babies in her hollow; rather than them being lost in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/149046-antagonistic-courts-or-entitlements?p=149089#post149089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's the Sun and Moon Courts, whose respective emotions are Disgust and Shame. They're most common in Slavic nations, I think, but have some very cool stuff going on; the Sun Court is full of massive assholes who want to judge everyone, while the Moon Court just enjoys reveling in being disgusting monsters. I'm quite fond of them both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course; the entire point of the Sun and Moon Court is that they balance each other out to create a nice Freehold. Doesn't always work though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T21:17:41-07:00","id":151016,"title":"","content":"Another idea that might suit your needs is having multiple, mutually antagonistic freeholds in your city. Local changelings could have any number of reasons to establish separate ones, from past feuds and slights that transcended any single Court, to their city being plain too big for one freehold (Lords of Summer established Los Angeles as having four). You could have a similar setup, with one of the freeholds being dominated by nasty leaders, an arrangement with the True Fae, or some other quality that sets them up as enemies.<br /> <br /> If you want to make this a behind the scenes thing, perhaps the other freehold hasn't been founded yet, but its would-be members are nearly ready to break off from the parent freehold. Your players could initially cross paths with changeling secessionists from one Court, only to eventually discover a much larger conspiracy that spans all four.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T20:29:30-07:00","id":152048,"title":"","content":"If you want an antagonistic entitlement I'd have to go with the Parliament of victors, they can easily become one of the most narcissistic, bullheaded people who back their own behaviors by actually having the power behind their talk. Think of a greek demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}